    dict(key='17-costs', kind='bullets', title='What It Costs',
         body=['Names cannot be parameters:', '  a sort column needs a fixed list', 'Parameters protect values, not the whole design', 'Least privilege needs a database user per job', 'Detailed error messages help attackers'],
         narration='Nothing is free. [[slnc 400]] Here is what the defences cost. [[slnc 500]] A parameter can carry a value, but never a name. [[slnc 300]] So a sort column or a table name must be picked from a fixed list in the code. [[slnc 500]] Parameters protect the values in a statement, but a query that is built badly in other ways still needs care. [[slnc 500]] Least privilege means a separate database user for each job, and someone has to manage those users. [[slnc 500]] And a detailed database error shown on the page teaches an attacker how the statement looks, so errors stay in the log.'),
